# Backend Rules Index

Define backend technical standards for `hms-backend`.

## Conflict order
1. security, privacy, safety, and compliance rules
2. [`.cursor/api-contract.mdc`](../../.cursor/api-contract.mdc) for cross-stack HTTP behavior
3. the owner file named below
4. other backend rule files
5. backend dev-plan files

## Backend-wide invariants
- Express.js and CommonJS are mandatory.
- Database objects, Prisma models, and documented payload fields use lowercase `snake_case`.
- Public APIs and realtime payloads expose `human_friendly_id` only; never return raw primary keys.
- Effective access = `union(role, module, user grants) ∩ active subscription ∩ assigned modules ∩ ABAC scope`; no grant bypasses subscription limits.
- Default modules, packages, roles, and permissions live in `.cursor/access/`; admin changes are versioned and auditable.
- Every business module must stay standalone and entitlement-aware.
- Public APIs and complex logic require JSDoc documentation.
- Circular dependencies are forbidden.

## Owner map
- `architecture.mdc`: runtime, layering, dependency direction
- `project-structure.mdc`: folder and script ownership
- `coding-standards.mdc`: naming, comments, reuse
- `import-aliases.mdc`: aliases and import boundaries
- `module-creation.mdc`: module build sequence
- `api.mdc`, `api-versioning.mdc`, `response-format.mdc`, `validation.mdc`: HTTP contract
- `auth-security.mdc`: authn, authz, ABAC, break-glass
- `.cursor/access/*.mdc`: default access (cross-stack)
- `cors.mdc`, `rate-limiting.mdc`, `health-checks.mdc`, `error-logging.mdc`, `constants-env.mdc`: runtime safety
- `prisma.mdc`, `storage.mdc`, `websockets.mdc`, `performance.mdc`, `offline-support.mdc`, `internationalization.mdc`: platform behavior
- `compliance.mdc`, `documentation.mdc`, `testing.mdc`: governance
